  "generated_text": "1. Identify the first term \\( a \\) and the common ratio \\( r \\) of the geometric sequence.\n2. Use the formula for the \\( n \\)-th term of a geometric sequence: \\( a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1} \\).\n3. Given the fifth term \\( a_5 = 162 \\), we can write:\n   \\[\n   162 = 2 \\cdot r^4\n   \\]\n4. Solve for \\( r \\):\n   \\[\n   r^4 = \\frac{162}{2} = 81\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   r = \\sqrt[4]{81} = 3\n   \\]\n5. Now, find the sixth term \\( a_6 \\) using the formula:\n   \\[\n   a_6 = 2 \\cdot r^5\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( r = 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   a_6 = 2 \\cdot 3^5 = 2 \\cdot 243 = 486\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{486}\n\\]\n\\]",
